+The name stuck: "Impressionists." At first it meant painters who offered only an impression — a first glance rather than a properly finished picture. But the artists gradually accepted the name and turned the insult into an identity. That’s what "Impressionist" means in this story: not one strict style, but artists connected by these independent exhibitions and by a shared willingness to show modern life through visible, immediate ways of painting.
 
